    "body": "# PR type\n\n- [x] Bug Fix\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Document Updates\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\n\n# PR information\n\nAlpha-divergence DPO can produce NaN/Inf even when the loss and gradients are representable. With FP16 sequence log-probabilities of -44 for both policy responses and -20 for both reference responses, alpha=0.5 and beta=0.1, the loss becomes NaN instead of log(2). The exponent cap itself overflows while rounding in FP16. Separately, dividing the exponential difference by alpha before multiplying by beta can overflow an otherwise finite scaled margin, including in FP32.\n\nThis patch:\n\n- Computes the exponent cap with Python math, outside the input tensor's low precision.\n- Promotes FP16/BF16 sequence log-probabilities to FP32 before the alpha-divergence calculation, preserving FP64 inputs.\n- Applies beta/alpha together for losses using the scaled margin; retains the unscaled margin required by IPO.\n\nOnly sequence-level tensors are promoted. This PR contains one production file; the additional numerical regression tests remain local at the submitter's request. It addresses these two overflow paths, not general cancellation near alpha=0 or every possible extreme input.\n\nRelated: #10313 fixes DiscoPOP's modulated exponential, a different loss branch. Searches for open PRs referencing #10313, `_get_exp_cap`, or `alpha_divergence` found no duplicate alpha-divergence fix.\n\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex implemented the patch and ran the validation below. Human review/attestation items remain unchecked.\n\n## Experiment results\n\nCPU; Python 3.12.13, PyTorch 2.13.0+cu130, Transformers 5.14.1, TRL 0.29.1.\n\nExisting tests, with two independently confirmed baseline failures deselected:\n\n```bash\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/test_align/test_rlhf_loss.py \\\n  tests/test_align/test_dpo_exo_loss.py \\\n  tests/utils/test_dpo_precompute.py \\\n  --deselect='tests/test_align/test_rlhf_loss.py::test_padding_free_dpo_matches_padded[True]' \\\n  --deselect=tests/test_align/test_rlhf_loss.py::TestPackedRLHFReduction::test_padding_free_dpo_logits_to_keep_ld_integration -q\n```\n\nResult: **18 passed, 33 subtests passed, 2 deselected**. Both deselected cases fail on the upstream base and this patch because their fixture lacks `tuner_backend`; the unrestricted suite was also run.\n\nAdditional local-only validation:\n\n- 36 numerical subcases covering exponent caps, FP16/BF16 overflow, FP32 scaling overflow, FP64 preservation, smoothing, and sigmoid/robust/EXO/hinge/IPO values and gradients against independent FP64 references: all passed; 13 subcases fail on the upstream base.\n- A trainable FP32 linear head with FP16 logits and 64-token log-probability sums: loss **0.6931471825**, all parameter gradients finite, maximum parameter-gradient difference from the same forward with an FP64 loss **0**. A clipped SGD update remained finite. This is a synthetic correctness check, not a pretrained-model quality evaluation or GPU training run.\n- `pre-commit run --all-files`: all hooks passed; `git diff --check`: passed.\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] I have linked the related issue above, if there is one.\n- [ ] I have reviewed and understand every changed line, and I can explain how the change works and why it is correct.\n- [ ] I have run the relevant tests or reproductions locally, and included the commands and results above (if applicable).\n- [ ] I am responsible for the content of this PR, regardless of how it was produced.\n",
